  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the clear best at 0.7062 acc, outperforming the resnet50 variant (config_001, 0.6776) by ~3% and the RNA-only baseline (config_002, 0.6501) by ~5.6%. This establishes that the VIT-L image encoder + weighted fusion + multiprofile setup is the strongest direction. Uncertainty: whether the simple avgpool aggregation is the bottleneck for combining multiple profiles, or whether a learned transformer aggregation could capture richer inter-profile interactions. This experiment tests that single change: replacing avgpool with transformer aggregation while keeping the proven weighted fusion and VIT-L encoder. It is the best next step because it directly extends the best configuration along the most impactful untested axis (aggregation mechanism), and a transformer over profiles could yield a meaningful accuracy gain. Expected cost: moderate-to-high (~6-7 GPU hours) due to the transformer aggregation layer on top of the VIT-L multimodal pipeline, somewhat above config_008's 4.82 hrs, but justified by the high expected accuracy ceiling."
}

